WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.710
So last night was the second night of the
Democratic National Convention, we had a live

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.590
stream for the full two hours.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:11.959
There was the sort of formal nomination process
of Joe Biden with each state casting their

00:00:11.959 --> 00:00:16.820
delegates proportionally or 100 percent for
different candidates.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.660
And it was a significantly better night.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.290
The night won, without question.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:27.040
There were fewer of these energy sucking moments
were after like an okay speech.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.180
They would cut to low energy, smooth jazz
or something like that.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.439
It was better put together.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:37.550
There were actually some very interesting
moments headlined by Joe Biden's wife, Dr.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.800
Jill Biden, who did the last speech of the
night, who I realized in watching her she

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.000
would be a better president than Donald Trump.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.280
Forget about Joe Biden for a moment.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:53.220
I was trying to think, is there any issue
where if you said, David, we need either Donald

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.980
Trump or Jill Biden to figure out this issue,
is there any issue or I would pick Donald

00:00:58.980 --> 00:00:59.980
Trump and there really isn't.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:04.979
I mean, even on Corona virus, quite frankly,
it's hard to imagine anyone doing a worse

00:01:04.979 --> 00:01:07.570
job than drunk Trump on the virus.

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:12.000
But as a doctor of education, Jill Biden would
just understand.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.750
Oh, it's a medical situation.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:17.780
Oh, well, we need to let doctors take the
lead rather than than Donald Trump, for example.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.830
But I'm heading at getting ahead of myself
a little bit here.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:26.280
One of the best moments was one of the best
lines of the night, really was former Secretary

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.250
of State John Kerry referring to Donald Trump's
overseas trips as blooper reels.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:32.810
Take a look at this.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:36.590
Donald Trump inherited a growing economy and
a more peaceful world.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:40.900
And like everything else he inherited, he
bankrupted it.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.640
When this president goes overseas, it isn't
a goodwill mission.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:45.200
It's a blooper reel.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.580
He breaks up with our allies and writes love
letters to dictators.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.780
America deserves a president who is looked
up to not laugh.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.580
That that actually made me laugh in the moment.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:02.880
And John Kerry was was quite good at laying
out the importance of voting for Joe Biden

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.759
and to remove Donald Trump in November.

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:08.280
Bill Clinton also spoke and it was fine.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:12.940
There was debate about whether Bill Clinton
should speak or maybe instead it should be

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:18.480
Al Gore who is sort of a direct testament
to what happens when not enough people vote

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.760
and you end up winning the popular vote, losing
the Electoral College and changing the course

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.760
of history.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.260
Maybe Al Gore should have spoken instead.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:29.430
Maybe Al Gore should or should have spoken
in addition to Bill Clinton.

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:34.090
We heard from Congresswoman Alexandria Cosio
Cortez in a much anticipated speech.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.430
It was very short.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:38.849
She formally nominated Bernie Sanders to be
the nominee.

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:41.920
There were some people who said, oh, it's
a snub.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.510
It was really a formality.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.770
Bernie was set to receive delegates from some
states, so someone has to nominate him.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:49.870
It was not a snub.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:51.710
It was rather procedural.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:58.910
And NBC News took some heat because they misreported
what Alexandria, Cosio, Cortez did and they

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.370
made a big deal out of it.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:04.629
I'm not going to since it really wasn't a
big deal and I don't want to play into that.

00:03:04.629 --> 00:03:07.190
But we did hear from AOC and then.

00:03:07.190 --> 00:03:08.190
Yeah.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:12.290
Dr. Jill Biden, let's take a look at just
a little bit of her speech and you'll see

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:15.769
this is the wrap up and you'll see Joe Biden
come out and embrace her.

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:20.519
If you're watching and you'll hear him say
just a few words if you are listening.

00:03:20.519 --> 00:03:29.660
I know that if we entrust this nation to Joe,
he will do for your family what he did for

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:39.240
ours, bring us together and make us whole
carry us forward in our time of need.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:48.180
Keep the promise of America for all of us.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.590
Hi, everyone.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:54.590
I'm Joe Barton.

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:56.129
Salzman has heard, you know.

00:03:56.129 --> 00:04:00.680
Excuse me, you can see why she's the love
of my life, the rock of our family.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:02.750
She never gives herself much credit.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.790
But the truth is, she's the strongest person
I know.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.930
She's a backbone, like a ramrod.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.430
She loves fiercely, cares deeply.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.810
Nothing stops her when she sets her mind and
getting something right.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:17.199
So, yeah, I mean, it's all pretty cheesy.

00:04:17.199 --> 00:04:20.810
This this isn't the type of packaging that
appeals to me.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.189
This isn't the type of political event that
appeals to me.

00:04:24.189 --> 00:04:25.749
But it doesn't matter.

00:04:25.749 --> 00:04:27.259
I'm not the target here.

00:04:27.259 --> 00:04:29.350
And realistically, neither are you.

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:34.569
Realistically, anybody who is watching the
David Pakman show on YouTube listens to political

00:04:34.569 --> 00:04:35.569
podcasts.

00:04:35.569 --> 00:04:37.129
If you listen to the podcast.

00:04:37.129 --> 00:04:38.339
You're not the target.

00:04:38.339 --> 00:04:39.419
You've already decided.

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:40.419
Right.

00:04:40.419 --> 00:04:42.490
And so I think it's important for us to keep
that in mind.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:49.969
But I have to say, when you hear about and
learn about the tragedy of Joe Biden's life,

00:04:49.969 --> 00:04:57.430
losing his first wife and child in a car accident,
and then you hear about Jill Biden becoming

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:02.949
a mother to Joe Biden's two sons while she
was in graduate school, you just see the way

00:05:02.949 --> 00:05:04.809
the Bidens relate to each other.

00:05:04.809 --> 00:05:09.800
It is a reminder because of the stark contrast
that's in the White House right now about

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:16.050
how absurd the Trump administration and Trump
as president is.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:19.569
On a personal level, Malana seems to hate
Trump.

00:05:19.569 --> 00:05:22.460
Some of Trump's kids seem to hate him.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:26.680
Trump seems to think some of his kids are
idiots, like none.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.979
None of this is normal.

00:05:27.979 --> 00:05:30.330
And obviously we can separate.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:35.360
You know, if their politics are great, who
cares about their home lives in this particular

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.969
case with Donald Trump?

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.909
It's all related and it's all very, very bad.

00:05:39.909 --> 00:05:45.559
The same delusions of grandeur and narcissism
that make his personal life and family life

00:05:45.559 --> 00:05:49.300
a disaster, make his administration a disaster.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:54.210
And that was you know, I didn't really need
the convention because the choices are so

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.059
crystal clear for me this time around.

00:05:57.059 --> 00:06:02.240
But I do think that this second night, particularly
with Dr. Jill Biden and some of the backstory

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:08.860
on Joe Biden's life, I do think it actually
was far better put together the night, number

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:09.860
one.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:13.430
So tonight we're going to be hearing from
Senator Elizabeth Warren, which I'm very much

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:14.539
looking forward to.

00:06:14.539 --> 00:06:19.369
Again, as someone who competed against Joe
Biden in the Democratic primary this year.

00:06:19.369 --> 00:06:25.330
We heard from by Bernie on Monday night making
the case that if you supported Bernie in 2016,

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.569
if you supported Bernie in 2020.

00:06:27.569 --> 00:06:31.060
Here is why it is so important to vote for
Joe Biden in November.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:36.810
I'm interested to see how Elizabeth Warren
puts together a sort of similar argument.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:42.699
I'm not as much looking forward to hearing
from Nancy Pelosi and Hillary Clinton tonight,

00:06:42.699 --> 00:06:47.429
although I think it will be interesting to
see what approach they take and whether they

00:06:47.429 --> 00:06:50.379
play to the left or they play to the middle
or what they do.

00:06:50.379 --> 00:06:55.289
We're going to hear from former Congresswoman
Grap Gabby Giffords, who is a tragically was

00:06:55.289 --> 00:06:59.729
a victim of gun violence years ago and also
headlining tonight.

00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:02.789
We will hear from vice presidential candidate
Kamala Harris.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:07.319
And we're also going to hear form from former
President Barack Obama.

00:07:07.319 --> 00:07:13.779
All leading up to the final night tomorrow
when we will hear from the nominee himself,

00:07:13.779 --> 00:07:14.969
Joe Biden.

00:07:14.969 --> 00:07:19.960
And it's much anticipated for different reasons
by different people.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:25.289
The right is anticipating Joe Biden's speech
with the idea that he's going to be a barely

00:07:25.289 --> 00:07:32.580
coherent and unable to put together anything
sensible or so or sensical, whereas I'm interested

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:38.039
in seeing what is the approach in order to
bring people in.

00:07:38.039 --> 00:07:44.439
In other words, centrists, center left, disaffected
Republicans, progressive leftists, former

00:07:44.439 --> 00:07:47.620
Berney people, so on and so forth.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:54.409
So I will see you tonight at eight, 45 p.m.
Eastern Time on YouTube, twitch and or Facebook

00:07:54.409 --> 00:07:58.779
your preference for the start of night three.

00:07:58.779 --> 00:08:03.619
And we will be back, of course, tomorrow with
analysis and preparation for the final night

00:08:03.619 --> 00:08:05.689
of the Democratic National Convention.

00:08:05.689 --> 00:08:08.830
And then we have to get ready for the Republican
National Convention happening next week.

